Revenue Transfer Impact Simulator
A single-file tool (no install, runs in any browser) that lets a manager preview how a proposed account-ownership transfer changes both reps' Predicted Year-End Revenue Attainment, before the change is made in Anaplan.
What it needs
An Excel export with these columns present somewhere in the file (column order and exact position don't matter — the tool detects them by header name):
Account
Patch (current owner)
Planning Country
Revenue Quota By Account
Revenue Credit
A New Owner column is optional — include it to pre-assign proposed transfers before upload.
What it does
Auto-detects the header row and matches columns by name, not fixed position
Shows a Team Overview (before → after) for every rep affected
Lets you fine-tune any assignment manually via Manager Override, on top of what was pre-assigned in Excel
Calculates Predicted Year-End Revenue Attainment for each rep, before and after
Exports a full CSV of every account with its current owner, pre-assigned owner, manager override, and final effective owner — so nothing is lost between what was uploaded and what was decided in the tool
What it does NOT do
Simulation only. Nothing is written back to Anaplan — Sales Ops still keys the approved transfer in manually, by design, so there's a human checkpoint before any system-of-record change.
Data note
The sample data in this repo is fully synthetic — no real account names, rep names, or company data. Use `anonymize_excel.py` in this repo to de-identify your own export before uploading it here.
